Eric, 2026-10-07: "get familiar with the new matt pocock skills and defer to those
for necessary invocation when needed."

**Why:** He upgraded to 1.3.1 from Matt's own marketplace the same day (see
[[skill-bloat-and-promotion]]) and wants those skills, not near-duplicates, to drive the work.

**How to apply:** when a task fits, invoke the `mattpocock-skills:` skill first. On overlap:

| Task | Use | Instead of |
|---|---|---|
| Bug, error, slow code | `diagnosing-bugs` (tight red loop first) | `superpowers:systematic-debugging` |
| Test-first build/fix | `tdd` (agree seams with Eric first) | `superpowers:test-driven-development` |
| Stress-test a plan | `grilling` (rounds, recommended answers) | `superpowers:brainstorming` Q&A |
| Edit a skill, CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md | `writing-for-agents` | `superpowers:writing-skills` |
| Module/interface design | `codebase-design` | — |
| Glossary / ADR / domain terms | `domain-modeling` | — |
| Throwaway logic or UI test | `prototype` | — |
| Docs/API fact-finding to a .md | `research` (background agent) | — |
| PR body | `pr` (Summary / Evidence / Merge Danger) | — |
| Steps only a human can do | `wizard` (bash script) | — |

Eric, later 2026-10-07: "I want to default all the mattpocock skills." Every overlapping skill
is now "off" in `~/.claude/settings.json` skillOverrides: built-in `code-review`; superpowers
`requesting-code-review`, `test-driven-development`, `systematic-debugging`, `brainstorming`,
`writing-skills`, `writing-plans` (→ `/to-spec`), `executing-plans` and
`subagent-driven-development` (→ `/implement-spec`), `finishing-a-development-branch` (→ `pr`);
`anthropic-skills:skill-creator` (→ `writing-for-agents`), `anthropic-skills:deep-research` (→ `research`).

Exceptions:
- `mattpocock-skills:code-review` is ON (Eric's choice). It needs `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md`;
  run `/setup-matt-pocock-skills` once per repo. `codex-review` stays as the Codex reviewer.
- Owned skills are not set "off" (portability rule): `CreateSkill` and `session-handoff` stay.
- Eric's own domain skills still win in their lane (status-report, research-in-5, etc.).
- Eric is usage-sensitive: `grilling` and `research` may spawn sub-agents; keep it to one.
- Slash-only (Eric runs them): `/grill-me`, `/grill-with-docs`, `/to-spec`, `/to-tickets`,
  `/implement`, `/implement-spec`, `/triage`, `/wayfinder`, `/handoff`, `/teach`,
  `/to-questionnaire`, `/wait-what`, `/retro`, `/ask-matt`, `/improve-codebase-architecture`,
  `/setup-matt-pocock-skills` (run once per repo before the tracker-based skills).
  Suggest one by name when it fits.
